# SPA fallback. Every route is served by index.html and resolved client-side by
# React Router, so a HARD navigation to a deep link -- opening /clients in a new
# tab, or just pressing refresh -- must not be answered with a 404.
#
# render.yaml declares this same rewrite, but the frontend service was not built
# from that manifest, so the rule never existed in production: the root URL worked
# (Render serves index.html there by default) and every other path returned "Not
# Found". It broke the "Add a new client" link, which opens /clients in a new tab,
# and refresh on any page.
#
# Keeping it HERE rather than only in the dashboard means it is versioned, reviewed
# and cannot be lost the next time the service is recreated.
/*    /index.html   200
